{"_v":1,"id":"grease-2007","cs":52,"rc":5,"bd":{"positive":0,"mixed":3,"negative":2},"rv":[{"cn":"Elisabeth Vincentelli","o":"New York Post","s":69,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.nypost.com/p/entertainment/theater/there_but_for_the_grace_of_god_or_cx963SRmkYip6ZvaVwXbcL","q":"Grace veers off in interesting directions by moving all the characters outside of their comfort zone."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":41,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"http://theater.nytimes.com/2007/08/20/theater/reviews/20grea.html","d":"2007-08-20","q":"Those who come to 'Grease' without such sentimental attachments are sure to be baffled by the lack of wit, charisma or original presence on the stage."},{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"The New York Times","s":37,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2007/08/20/theater/reviews/20grea.html","d":"2007-08-20","q":"But there’s the numbing sense of performers of undeveloped talent conscientiously doing what they have been told to do and failing to claim their parts as their own."},{"cn":"Matt Windman","o":"amNewYork","s":66,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.amny.com/urbanite-1.812039/theater-review-grace-2-5-stars-1.4076388","q":"Even if many of the scenes drag, Wright does raise some provocative questions about religion, especially as Rudd's character attempts to justify his disastrous situation and unwavering faith."},{"cn":"Elijah Gonzalez","o":"The A.V. Club","s":70,"b":"Positive","t":3,"u":"http://www.avclub.com/tvclub/better-or-worse-grease-live-revolutionizes-live-tv-231541","q":"An odd mix of revolutionary presentation and too-familiar staging, Grease: Live was a confident, competent three hours of musical theater."}],"au":{"score":69,"designation":"Shrugging","sources":{"mz":{"s":69,"c":62,"sr":3.5}}},"hi":"/images/shows/grease-2007/hero.webp","ta":"256 W 47th St, New York, NY 10036","pd":"2007-07-24","ca":[{"n":"Max Crumm","r":"Danny Zuko"},{"n":"Laura Osnes","r":"Sandy Dumbrowski"},{"n":"Ryan Patrick Binder